# Witness data for testing the Rudvalis binary normal forms

Each negative row gives one separating point. Each positive row gives a product
of defining generators of one candidate and a word conjugating it to the marked
generator. These are untrusted witnesses; the descendants check their assertions.

Source: `ElementaryCatalogue/source/certificates.json`, generated from the
preserved ATLAS words by `source/Generate.g`. The inverse point convention
preserves multiplication; the precise conventions and attribution are in
`ElementaryCatalogue/source/README.md`. See also GLS3 Table 5.3r and quasithin
printed p.511, citing [Asc86b]. This concrete word calculation is not itself
stated on either book page.
-/

